figdown 0.1 block
# §5: the presentation attributes are optional on ANY element that can
# carry them — one document exercising every construct that takes them.
# 0.1 (`STYLE-KEY-SCOPE`): `style=` left `field`, `cell` and `signal`, so those
# three lines carry `fill=`/`stroke=` only. See 305 for the carve-out.
#
# 0.3 (`PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`): `plane=` was WITHDRAWN with the `plane` keyword, so the
# §5 set is four attributes, not five, and every ` plane=over` that stood on
# the `class`, `external`, `group`, `node`, `edge`, `bundle`, `threshold` and
# `band` lines below is gone. The `plane over "Overlay" z-index=3`
# declaration those keys referenced stood on the line after `title` and went
# with them. One consequence is visible in the source: `external` had
# `plane=` as its ONLY option key, so it now carries no §5 attribute at all
# and appears here purely as the target of `edge a -> wire`.
# `bundle bd "LAG"` is in section 2, because `bundle` is declared by
# `topology` only since `SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP` — its presentation row is still exercised.
title "Presentation attributes, everywhere"
class hot "Hot path" fill=#fee2e2 stroke=#dc2626 style=dashed
external wire "to the wire"
group g "Group" fill=#f6f5ef stroke=#94a3b8 style=dotted
node a "A" in=g fill=#dbeafe stroke=#1d4ed8 style=dashed
node b "B" in=g class=hot
edge a [tx] -[mid]-> [hx] b stroke=#059669 style=dotted
edge a -> wire
threshold "cap" in=g offset=70% stroke=#b45309 style=dotted
band "zone" 10..40% in=g fill=#e0f2fe stroke=#0369a1 style=dashed
bitfield bf "Bits" word=16 fill=#f8fafc stroke=#334155 numbering=lsb0
field "One" 4 fill=#fde68a stroke=#b45309
field "Two" 12
table t "Table" fill=#f8fafc stroke=#475569
| h | i |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
cell (1,1) fill=#fee2e2 stroke=#dc2626
timing w "Wave" fill=#ecfeff stroke=#0e7490
signal clk p... fill=#fef9c3 stroke=#a16207

figdown 0.1 topology
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -- b
bundle bd "LAG" a--b stroke=#7c3aed style=dotted
